# givenchy-scraper — configuration
# ---------------------------------
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not, so it
# must never hold a real value.
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# These four names are exactly what `env_config.ENV_KEYS` reads — no more and
# no fewer. A variable that is not here is not read, and a variable here that
# the code does not read is a setting that looks configurable and is not.
#
# Credentials live HERE and nowhere else. Never pass one on the command line:
# `--proxy http://user:pass@host` becomes part of the process's argv, which
# anyone able to run `ps` can read, and it lands in shell history too.
#
# PLACEHOLDERS: leave a line as it is below to mean "unset". `env_config`
# recognises `your_2captcha_api_key_here` and a `{braced}` word as
# unfilled and treats the variable as absent. That matters more than it
# looks: a braced placeholder copied into a live `.env` otherwise reads as
# CONFIGURED and produces an authentication error a long way from its cause.


# 2Captcha API key. One key, four separately-billed products: captcha
# solving, the Scraping Browser API, proxies and fingerprints.
# Get it from https://2captcha.com/enterpage
TWOCAPTCHA_KEY=your_2captcha_api_key_here

# Scraping Browser API endpoint — a remote browser this repo connects to over
# CDP instead of launching one locally (`--cdp-endpoint`).
#
#   ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-{cc}-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222
#
# `country-` picks the exit country, which on this site decides which
# storefront and currency you are served; `pid-` is a profile with persistent
# cookies and allows ONE live connection each, so two runs sharing a pid fail
# with `profile_locked`. Reuse pids rather than minting one per run.
#
# Selenium cannot use this: chromedriver's `debuggerAddress` takes a bare
# host:port with nowhere to put a password. Playwright and pyppeteer can.
#
# Fetch or refresh one with:
#   python3 tools/browser_profile_client.py accounts
#   python3 tools/browser_profile_client.py use --account-id N --write-env
GIVENCHY_CDP_ENDPOINT=

# A single proxy for `--proxy`, as a full URL with credentials:
#   http://LOGIN:PASSWORD@proxy.2captcha.com:PORT
# For a pool, use `--proxy-file proxylist.txt` (gitignored) or
# `--proxy-sessions N` to mint session-pinned exits from this one credential.
GIVENCHY_PROXY=

# A default `--url`. Useful for a scheduled run that always reads the same
# listing. Leave empty to build the URL from --category and --site-locale.
#   https://www.givenchybeauty.com/us/makeup/lips/
GIVENCHY_URL=
